# PLAN-911 native source-diagnostic suite — the typed fact channel for the
# M1 B17/B18/B19 negatives. Every ac-native leg runs the REAL scalar worker
# in the explicit `source-v1` observation mode (`mn.diagnostics`): the
# parent admits the worker's `mn.source-diagnostic/1` fact on the raw wire
# bytes BEFORE comparing against the expected face, so these checks verify
# the real shared-compiler cause (raw stage/code), never a generic shell.
#
#   negatives  src/B17|B18|B19.at  — verify/source.type-mismatch,
#                                 verify/verify.immutable-write,
#                                 verify/verify.no-return-path (raw stage
#                                 `verify` → judged face `typecheck`)
#   neighbors  src/NB17|NB18|NB19.at — legal programs, real PE 2/2/0, and
#                                 the strict mode echo is itself admitted
#                                 (a worker silently ignoring the field
#                                 cannot pass)
#   variants   nd911-src/*.at — same-family shapes (the family is the CODE,
#                                 stable across shapes), a MULTIBYTE-comment
#                                 source (utf8-byte spans stay on char
#                                 boundaries past non-ASCII text),
#                                 the multi-cause
#                                 source (primary = the compiler's first
#                                 cause), and two OTHER-stage rejections
#                                 (Text → parse, Bind → resolve) that must
#                                 stay distinct from the three families.
#
# Protocol-level admission negatives (duplicate wire keys, forged primary,
# over-cap payloads, mixed result shapes) are parent-side unit controls
# (auto-lang-core ac_mn::source_diag_tests) — a mutating fixture cannot be
# a committed green case.

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "ace.m1.nd911.b17"
  tags: ["ace-m1", "diagnostic", "native-diags-911"]
  links: ["PLAN-911"]
  source: { file: "src/B17.at", syntax: "auto", path: "main.at" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "ac-native-strict", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: { recipe: "ac/mir-native-scalar-v1", mn: { entry: "d_main", diagnostics: "source-v1" }, steps: [{ op: "run" }] },
      expect: { completion: { stage: "typecheck", code: "source.type-mismatch" } } },
  ]
}
```

